Ta Dumbong Kro Aung Statue,here:pds:place:116w636k-fd8c11bff7ca426aa180ff8c199e9472,en,tourist_attraction,"{'label': 'Ta Dumbong Kro Aung Statue, ផ្លូវជាតិ 5, 021402 បាត់ដំបង, កម្ពុជា', 'countryCode': 'KHM', 'countryName': 'កម្ពុជា', 'county': 'បាត់ដំបង', 'city': 'បាត់ដំបង', 'district': 'ព្រែកព្រះស្ដេច', 'street': 'ផ្លូវជាតិ 5', 'postalCode': '021402'}","{'lat': 13.09054, 'lng': 103.20867}","[{'lat': 13.09054, 'lng': 103.20867}]",246986,"[{'id': '300-3000-0023', 'name': 'Tourist Attraction', 'primary': True}, {'id': '300-3000-0025', 'name': 'Historical Monument'}]",Not available,"[{'supplier': {'id': 'tripadvisor'}, 'id': '6599078'}]",[{'www': [{'value': 'http://battambangtrip.travel.blog/battambang-details'}]}],Not Available,Battambang,13.09054,103.20867,6599078,Ta Dumbong Kro Aung Statue,"Ta Dumbong Kro Aung Statue ( Black man Statue ) Founded in the 11th century by the Khmer Empire, Battambang is the leading rice-producing province of the country. For nearly 100 years it was a major commercial hub and provincial capital of Siamese province of Inner Cambodia (1795-1907), though it was always populated by Khmer, with some ethnic Vietnamese, Lao, Thai and Chinese. Battambang remains the hub of Cambodia’s northwest, connecting the region with Phnom Penh and Thailand.",https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g303666-d6599078-Reviews-Ta_Dumbong_Kro_Aung_Statue-Battambang_Battambang_Province.html?m=66827,"{'street1': '314 Cnr National Route 5 & Street', 'city': 'Battambang', 'state': 'Battambang Province', 'country': 'Cambodia', 'postalcode': '02000', 'address_string': '314 Cnr National Route 5 & Street, Battambang 02000 Cambodia'}","[{'level': 'City', 'name': 'Battambang', 'location_id': '303666'}, {'level': 'Province', 'name': 'Battambang Province', 'location_id': '2366626'}, {'level': 'Country', 'name': 'Cambodia', 'location_id': '293939'}]",Asia/Phnom_Penh,Not available,Not available,http://battambangtrip.travel.blog/battambang-details/,https://www.tripadvisor